  "assumptions": [
    "2.csv is a Spearman rank correlation matrix (recomputed from 1.csv: max abs diff 0.0478, corr 0.999965; median diff ~0) - statement 'Pearson' is a typo",
    "2.csv row/column order matches 1.csv feature order (corr2_map.csv: 209 named + 22 positional, positional agreement 100%)",
    "Median imputation (73/57750 cells, 0.13%) used only for recomputed cross-check and for downstream association matrices; 2.csv itself is used unmodified",
    "Graph threshold tau=0.30 affects only module narrative, not Top-3 selection (selection uses full matrices)",
    "Network is a cross-sectional co-expression (observational) graph; edges are not causal links"
  ],
  "equations": [
    "edge: |rho_ij| >= tau and q_bh_ij < 0.05 (Fisher z = arctanh(r)*sqrt(n_eff-3), BH over 26565 pairs, n_eff = pairwise complete rows from 1.csv)",
    "modularity Q = sum_c [ W_c / m - (K_c / 2m)^2 ], m = total edge weight",
    "module score s_k = mean over members of z-scored abundance; association = Spearman(s_k, target_dim)",
    "enrichment: Fisher exact (one-sided greater) of module membership x origin_paper, BH over tests"
  ],
  "algorithm": "2.csv (231x231 Spearman, mapped to 1.csv names via outputs/protocol/corr2_map.csv) -> |rho| threshold graph (tau_primary=0.30, pre-registered; statistical floor tau_FDR from BH q<0.05 with per-pair complete n_eff) -> weighted greedy modularity (Clauset-Newman-Moore) -> module enrichment vs 8.xlsx origin_paper (Fisher + BH) and module-score vs 50 sensory dims (Spearman + BH); spectral clustering (sklearn SpectralClustering) as independent partition cross-check; collinearity diagnostics from 2.csv + recomputed Spearman (eigenvalues, condition number, |rho|>0.9 clusters); tau grid sensitivity.",
